SWEET touch events: IsDisplayIntegrated + IsBuiltIn (patch 0315, ALL-ON T-36, research 140): UIKit types a touch Direct only when the top digitizer event has IsDisplayIntegrated (0xb0019) set, otherwise Indirect (UIKitCore 0x188dc8934 [bin], RM-00968); SpringBoard's SBHomeGesturePanGestureRecognizer allows Direct touches only (0x1c5841a40 [bin], RM-00988), so our touches (flag never set [read 0058/0069]) scroll apps but can never start the home gesture. Now SweetHIDTouch::touch sets IsDisplayIntegrated = 1 on the collection and every child and IsBuiltIn = 1 on the collection (backboardd mirrors both from the incoming top event, RM-00996/00997). Event fields only, no hardware access.

--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/hid/SweetHID.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/hid/SweetHID.cpp
@@ -1289,6 +1289,14 @@
 		return;
 	}
 	collection->setIntegerValue(kIOHIDEventFieldDigitizerCollection, TRUE);
+	/*
+	 * patch 0315 (ALL-ON T-36, research 140): UIKit makes a touch Direct only when the TOP digitizer event has
+	 * IsDisplayIntegrated (0xb0019) set, else Indirect (UIKitCore 0x188dc8934, RM-00968); SpringBoard's home pan
+	 * allows Direct touches only (SB 0x1c5841a40, RM-00988), so without it no home gesture. backboardd copies
+	 * IsDisplayIntegrated + IsBuiltIn from the incoming top event (RM-00996/00997). Event fields only, no hardware.
+	 */
+	collection->setIntegerValue(kIOHIDEventFieldDigitizerIsDisplayIntegrated, 1);
+	collection->setIntegerValue(kIOHIDEventFieldIsBuiltIn, 1);
 
 	UInt32 cmask = 0;
 	for (int i = 0; i < SWEET_TOUCH_FINGERS; i++) {
@@ -1319,6 +1327,7 @@
 		child->setIntegerValue(kIOHIDEventFieldDigitizerIdentity, i + 2);
 		child->setIntegerValue(kIOHIDEventFieldDigitizerTouch, d);
 		child->setIntegerValue(kIOHIDEventFieldDigitizerEventMask, mask);
+		child->setIntegerValue(kIOHIDEventFieldDigitizerIsDisplayIntegrated, 1);   /* patch 0315 */
 		collection->appendChild(child);
 		child->release();
 		cmask |= mask;
